<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n58910" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόνῑσ-τρα</span></b> , ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>place covered with dust</i>:
			hence, <i>rolling place</i>, such as birds make in the dust,
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				613b9
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>arena in a wrestling school</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				867
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.638c
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρόμοι καὶ κ. καὶ γυμνάσια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					11.10
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				6.15
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Eust.
				382.32
			</span></i>; also in a theatre, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σκηνή</span>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
